    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded in 1347 when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> nobles rebelled against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-bin-tughluq">Muhammad bin Tughluq</a> and proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ala-ud-din-bahman-shah">Bahman Shah</a> sultan.</li><li>Its Persianate court ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalaburagi">Gulbarga</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bidar">Bidar</a> and fought Vijayanagara for 150 years over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raichur-doab">Raichur Doab</a>.</li><li>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-gawan">Mahmud Gawan</a>'s execution in 1481 its governors broke away, founding the five <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-sultanates">Deccan sultanates</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Russian merchant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afanasy-nikitin">Afanasy Nikitin</a> stayed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bidar">Bidar</a> around 1470 and wrote one of the earliest European descriptions of the Bahmani court and its people.</p></aside>
    </section>

