asa</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bidar">Bidar</a> is built</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1481</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-gawan">Mahmud Gawan</a> is executed on a forged charge of treason</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 1490</span><span class="rf-text">The governors of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bijapur">Bijapur</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmadnagar">Ahmadnagar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berar">Berar</a> become independent</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 1527</span><span class="rf-text">The last Bahmani sultan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalimullah-shah">Kalimullah</a>, flees <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bidar">Bidar</a></span></li></ol>
